Subject: Values of uiOutput elements reset when calling Shiny.bindAll()
Message-ID: <wPe6a4sP6tg.WzoDyoSMAgAJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shiny-discuss/c/wPe6a4sP6tg/m/WzoDyoSMAgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi

There seems to be more problems with the current unbindAll() bindAll() implementation (referring to https://groups.google.com/d/msg/shiny-discuss/kHUI5E9ZDvE/1aZR0mdlVNUJ).

The values of uiOutput elements are currently getting reset whenever Shiny.bindAll() is getting called in the client logic.

Example:

library(shiny)

runApp(list(
    ui = bootstrapPage(
      uiOutput("testSlider1"), br(),
      sliderInput("testSliderInput2", "testSliderInput2", 0, 100, 1, step = 1), br(),

      uiOutput("testText1"), br(),
      textInput("testTextInput2", "testTextInput2", value = "")
    ),
    server = function(input, output, session) {
      output$testSlider1 <- renderUI({
        sliderInput("testSliderInput1", "testSliderInput1", 0, 100, 1, step = 1)
      })

      output$testText1 <- renderUI({
        textInput("testTextInput1", "testTextInput1", value = "")
      })
    }
))

Open developers tools and call Shiny.unbindAll() followed by Shiny.bindAll() after altering any of the elements. Elements created using uiOutput will get reset whereas the others won't.

best

Thomas

